## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design offline-first real-time UI, combining fetch, WebSocket, Service Worker, and DOM strategies under production constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Cache-first fetch strategy for chat history and API endpoints
- WebSocket resilience with exponential backoff and reconnection
- Offline message queue persisted in IndexedDB
- Service Worker coordination with dynamic caching for messages
- Debounced, batched DOM rendering for performance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Sketch: service worker fetch handler with cache-first strategy
self.addEventListener('fetch', (e) => {
  if (e.request.method !== 'GET') return;
  e.respondWith(
    caches.match(e.request).then(r => r || fetch(e.request).then(res => {
      const clone = res.clone();
      caches.open('chat-v1').then(c => c.put(e.request, clone));
      return res;
    }))
  );
});
```

